s($,"cIs","cd1",()=>{var q="Stock",p="10 g coffee, 150 ml milk",o=t.s,n=t.dc,m=t.rj
return A.a([A.aN(A.a([A.U("Stock in the POS does four things:"),A.cz(A.a(["**Tracks the quantity** of every tracked item (pieces, grams or millilitres).","**Deducts on sale.** Sell a coffee and 10 g of coffee is deducted. Sell a cola and 1 piece is deducted.","**Warns you about what is running low.** The [[Stock]] icon shows a red number with the count of items under their minimum.","**Helps you order** and, once the goods arrive, adds them to stock with one tap."],o)),A.U("Open stock with the [[Stock]] icon in the main panel. Recipes and supplier orders are under [[Settings]] and in stock."),A.cI("Who can do what","Receiving goods, recipes and minimums are set by the owner or a manager with the price permission. Anyone on staff can open and send orders. Only the owner changes the ordering mode."),A.a_("How the manual is organised"),A.cz(A.a(["**Items and ingredients:** what can be tracked and how to create it.","**Receiving goods:** invoice photo, manual receipt, receiving from an order.","**Recipes:** automatic deduction of ingredients.","**Minimums and alerts:** when stock tells you to order.","**Ordering:** baskets, sending, receiving, modes.","**A normal day and troubleshooting.**"],o))],n),q,B.hH,"overview","What stock does and who can do what.","Stock overview"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("Everything in stock is an item. There are two kinds:"),A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Kind","Example","Sold at the till?"],o),A.a(["Sold item","Coca-Cola, waffles, water","Yes, it is in the sales grid"],o),A.a(["Ingredient","Bonomi coffee (g), milk (ml), lemons (g)","No, it is only used in recipes"],o)],m)),A.a_("How to create an item"),A.bc(A.a(["Open [[Stock]] and add a new item (or create it from an invoice photo).","Turn on **Track stock**. Without it the quantity is not tracked.","Choose the unit: **ks** (pieces), **g** or **ml**. Coffee and lemons are in grams, milk in millilitres.","For grams and millilitres fill in the **pack size** (milk 1000 ml, coffee 1000 g). Orders are counted in packs by it.","Fill in the **purchase price** and the **supplier**. The price is used on the goods receipt and for the portion margin.","For an ingredient turn off **Show in sales**, so it does not appear among the goods at the till."],o)),A.cJ("Coffee and lemons are not products for sale",'You sell an Espresso or a Latte, not "Bonomi". An ingredient must have Show in sales switched off, otherwise it appears in the till grid.')],n),q,B.n_,"items","A sold item or an ingredient, and how to create it.","Items and ingredients"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("When the supplier delivers, photograph the invoice or delivery note. The app reads the items from it and enters them into stock."),A.bc(A.a(["Open [[Stock]] and press [[Invoice from photo]].","Photograph the paper, or pick a photo from a file. Keep the paper flat, fully in frame and well lit.","Wait a few seconds. The app reads the supplier and the lines: name, quantity and price.","**Check every line.** Fix the quantity and price if the reading got them wrong. Delete lines you do not want.","Each line is matched to an existing item or becomes a new one. For ingredients (coffee, milk, lemons) leave [[Ingredient (not for sale)]] on, so they do not show up at the till.","Save. A goods receipt is created and the quantities are added to stock."],o)),A.cI("Protection against double entry","If an invoice from the same supplier was already entered in the last 60 days, the app asks whether to enter it again. If it is the same invoice, answer No."),A.cJ("Always check the reading","The photo is read by artificial intelligence and it can make mistakes, especially with blurry or crumpled paper. Before saving, compare at least the quantities with the paper."),A.U("Reading invoices needs an AI key entered in the settings. The owner enters it herself and never shares it with anyone.")],n),q,B.kY,"receiving-photo","The fastest way to get goods into stock.","Receiving from an invoice photo"),A.aN(A.a([A.a_("Manual goods receipt"),A.bc(A.a(["In [[Settings]] open [[Goods receipts and stock issues]].","Create a new goods receipt, choose the supplier and add items with quantities.","Save. Stock goes up."],o)),A.a_("From an order"),A.U("If you ordered through the app, press [[Goods arrived]] on the order after delivery. The goods receipt is created by itself from the ordered quantities. See the chapter on ordering."),A.cJ("Goods arrived differently than ordered","The button accepts the quantities from the order. If the supplier brought less or more, do not use it. Enter the goods through the invoice photo or a manual goods receipt with the real numbers."),A.a_("Fixing a mistake"),A.U("If you entered a wrong quantity, correct it with a stock issue or a new goods receipt in the opposite direction. Do not delete the original record, so the stock history stays clean.")],n),q,B.jm,"receiving-other","The other two ways to receive goods and how to fix a mistake.","Manual receiving, from an order, corrections"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("A recipe says how much of each ingredient is used when one piece is sold. Thanks to it, selling a coffee deducts both coffee and milk, and you do not count anything by hand."),A.a_("Recipes currently set up"),A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Sold item","Uses"],o),A.a(["Espresso","10 g coffee"],o),A.a(["Cappuccino",p],o),A.a(["Latte","10 g coffee, 200 ml milk"],o),A.a(["Iced coffee",p],o),A.a(["Filter coffee","10 g coffee"],o)],m)),A.U("The milk amounts are an estimate. If your own measuring gives something else, edit the recipe."),A.a_("How to create or change a recipe"),A.bc(A.a(["In [[Settings]] open [[Recipes]].","Choose the sold item (for example Latte).","Add a line, choose an ingredient and enter the amount in its unit: grams for coffee, millilitres for milk.","Add more lines for more ingredients. Remove a line you do not need.","Save. The next sale already deducts by the new recipe."],o)),A.cI("Portion cost and margin","On a recipe you see the cost of one portion and the margin. They are calculated from the purchase prices of the ingredients, so coffee and milk need an accurate price from the invoice."),A.a_("What a deduction looks like"),A.U("Example: you sell 5 espressos, 10 cappuccinos and 5 lattes. That is 20 coffees, so 200 g (0.200 kg) of coffee is deducted. When a sale is cancelled, the ingredients go back to stock. Do not mix grams and kilograms, always enter grams."),A.cJ("No recipe, no deduction","If you add a new drink and do not create a recipe, it sells but the ingredients in stock stay unchanged and the count will not match.")],n),q,B.kX,"recipes","What is deducted from stock when one drink is sold.","Recipes"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("The minimum is the quantity at which you should start ordering. It is set on each item."),A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Ingredient","Minimum"],o),A.a(["Bonomi coffee","400 g"],o),A.a(["Whole milk, 1 l","2 l"],o),A.a(["Lemons","200 g"],o)],m)),A.a_("What the alert looks like"),A.cz(A.a(["On the [[Stock]] icon in the main panel a red number appears: how many items are at or below their minimum.","In stock there is a red bar on top with the button [[Time to order: prepare the supplier order]].",'Depending on the ordering mode, a "running low" message with an Order button can also appear.'],o)),A.a_("How to change a minimum"),A.U("Open the item in stock, change the **Minimum** field and save. For grams and millilitres enter the base unit (1 litre = 1000 ml).")],n),q,B.n8,"minimums","When stock tells you to order.","Minimums and alerts"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("The orders screen is laid out in three steps from top to bottom. Staff just need to follow that order."),A.a_("How to get there"),A.U('[[Stock]], then [[Time to order: prepare the supplier order]]. Or the "running low" message and its Order button. Or [[Settings]], then [[Supplier orders]].'),A.a_("Step 1: Needs ordering"),A.U("The list of items at their minimum. For each you see how much is in stock, the minimum and which supplier it is from. The suggested quantity refills stock to twice the minimum, in whole packs."),A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Button","What it does"],o),A.a(["Add to order","The item goes into the started order of its supplier (the basket). Good when you want to wait and order several things at once."],o),A.a(["Order right away","A separate order with only this item is prepared and sending opens. Good when it is urgent."],o),A.a(["Add all to order","All items in the list at once into baskets by supplier."],o)],m)),A.a_("Step 2: Send the finished order to the supplier"),A.bc(A.a(["There is one started order for each supplier.","Change quantities with the plus and minus buttons. Lower a line to zero and it is removed from the order.","When the order is marked **Ready to send**, it has enough items. Press [[Send to supplier]].","The share sheet opens. Choose a message, e-mail or another app and send the order to the supplier."],o)),A.U("After sending, the order moves to step 3. The app never sends an order by itself, you always confirm the sending."),A.a_("Step 3: When the goods arrive"),A.bc(A.a(["Find the order that just arrived.","Check the goods against the delivery note.","Press [[Goods arrived]] and confirm. A goods receipt is created, stock goes up and the order disappears from the list."],o)),A.U("If needed, [[Send again]] sends the same text to the supplier once more.")],n),q,B.nf,"ordering","Needs ordering, send, goods arrived.","Ordering: three steps"),A.aN(A.a([A.U("At the top of the orders screen there is the card **Ordering mode**. Only the owner sees it."),A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Mode","Behaviour"],o),A.a(["Off","The app suggests and collects nothing. Stock alerts (the red number) keep working."],o),A.a(["Manual","You build orders yourself. Nothing is added automatically."],o),A.a(["Semi-automatic",'When an item drops to its minimum, a "running low" message appears with an Order button. This is the default mode.'],o),A.a(["Automatic","Items at their minimum are added to the supplier basket by themselves. You still confirm the sending."],o)],m)),A.U("Below the mode choice you set from how many items a basket is marked ready to send. The default is 3 items."),A.cI("Manual order","At the top of the screen there is the button [[Manual order]]. It is the older screen where you see all tracked items at once and fill in quantities by hand."),A.cI("Supplier on the item",'For an item to land in the right basket it must have a supplier filled in. Without one it ends up in the basket "No supplier". Suppliers are managed in the settings.')],n),q,B.eG,"ordering-modes","Off, manual, semi-automatic, automatic (owner only).","Ordering modes"),A.aN(A.a([A.dj(A.a([A.a(["When","What to do"],o),A.a(["Morning","Look at the red number on the Stock icon. If it shows, open the orders and decide what to order."],o),A.a(["During the day","Sell as usual. Ingredients are deducted by themselves from the recipes."],o),A.a(["When a delivery arrives","Photograph the invoice with Invoice from photo, check the lines and save. Or press Goods arrived on the order."],o),A.a(["Once a week","Count the key ingredients (coffee, milk) and compare with stock. Settle any difference with a stock issue or a goods receipt."],o)],m))],n),q,B.qH,"daily","What to do in the morning, during the day, on delivery and weekly.","A normal day"),A.aN(A.a([A.dj(A.a([A.a(["Problem","What to check"],o),A.a(["Coffee or lemons are in the till grid",'Open the item and turn off "Show in sales".'],o),A.a(["Ingredients were not deducted after a sale","Does the sold item have a recipe? Does the ingredient have stock tracking on?"],o),A.a(["The deduction is different from what you expect","Check the units in the recipe: g for coffee, ml for milk."],o),A.a(["The invoice photo is not read","Photograph again, better light, paper flat. Check that an AI key is entered in the settings."],o),A.a(["An invoice wants to be entered a second time","It is a safeguard. If it is the same invoice, answer No."],o),A.a(['An item does not show in "Needs ordering"',"Is it already in some order (started or sent)? Is the mode Off? Does the item have a minimum set?"],o),A.a(["Milk shows 0 in stock","Enter the first milk receipt. Until there is a receipt, stock shows zero and the till has nothing to deduct from."],o)],m))],n),q,B.n5,"troubleshooting","The most common problems and what to check.","When something is off")],t.HG)})
